  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EMERGENCY RESPONSE TO FOOD INSECURITY AND HOUSING FOR IDPs IN UPPER NILE</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Caritas diocese of Malakal, the humanitarian wing of the Catholic Diocese of Malakal, received pressing appeals for food relief and emergency sheltering for Makal County, including Malakal town and the UN Protection of Civilians site, in the Upper Nile State, South Sudan. Not, only that CTP  as funding agency also allocate some of the funds to cover hunger gap in  emergency food assistance in Panyikang County, where the Office is implementing a major Livelihoods  project in partnership with CTP. Because of priority given to project inputs of agriculture works, the &#x2018;food distribution&#x2019; component of the project was allocated a very limited budget. The population in Panyikang County are badly affected by the floods for the last 2 years 2020 to 2021 with little yield from their gardens several villages.  The population has no alternative of  overcoming the lean season until the next harvest without external support of providing them with food rationing.</narrative>
  </description>
